 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Stairs are tricky. Can he climb a flight of stairs without getting too out of breath? Then have him climb a few steps at a time with you holding the rail. Short sharp climbs are easier than long ones. Yes, a chair with a wide base and no wheels is ideal. It gives people confidence you' right there with them. Keep the room well lit and avoid shadows. A fold down chair and a cup of tea waiting can make a huge difference. Your granddad will be so touched.",
